  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Steppin** (1 review): Reviewer says the Steppin' section should be listed as Steppin into a Relax tease and back into Steppin', and calls it hot [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **announcer**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Got Soul**: rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n- **Relax(tease)**: rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2009-02-07** (recommended): audience recording; 13 songs; 112 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Occasional distortion on drum and vocal mics originated in the PA, so it also appears on the recording [1]\n- **soulive2009-02-07.flac24**: audience recording; 11 songs; 112 min [2]. Said about its sound: Occasional distortion on drum and vocal mics came from the PA, so it is also on the recording [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The show was a benefit for Celebrate Brooklyn; Cochema \"Cheme\" Gastelum guested on sax for some songs; uploader took photos [1]\n- The show was a benefit for Celebrate Brooklyn, with Cochema \"Cheme\" Gastelum guesting on sax on starred songs [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2009-02-07**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Audience [1]\n- **soulive2009-02-07.flac24**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Audience [2]. Also: This is the 24-bit fileset; a separate 16-bit version exists for streaming, CD burning and MP3 downloads [2]",
